    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In ancient Greece, there was a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "philosopher",
            "ref": "v-philosopher"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " named "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Socrates",
            "zh": "苏格拉底"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". He had a student named "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Plato",
            "zh": "柏拉图"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". One day, Plato asked his teacher what love was."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Socrates said, “Go across this field and bring back the best "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "wheat",
            "ref": "v-wheat"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". You can’t go "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "backwards",
            "ref": "v-backwards"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and you only have one chance.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After a long time, the student came back with nothing. Sadly, he said, “I did see the best wheat plant. But I was always thinking that there would be some better ones ahead. So I gave it up. As I moved on, there was nothing better than the one that came before.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Socrates replied, “This is love. It’s the best thing that can happen to us. But we usually don’t realize its value until it’s gone.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A few days later, Plato asked Socrates what happiness was. Socrates told his student to go across the field again and pick the most beautiful flower this time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Soon afterwards, Plato returned with a pretty flower. He said with a smile, “When I walked across the field, I saw this flower and picked it. Even though there were many other beautiful flowers, I still believed this was the prettiest one.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Then Socrates said, “This is happiness. It’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "being content with",
            "ref": "v-be-content-with"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " what you have, even when you know there are better ones out there.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
